    "description": "Buổi 45 theo syllabus FLM.",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">AIC211 · Chapter 9 · Session 45</span>\n<h2>Session 45 — Basic Deep Learning and NLP for Cybersecurity</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14523 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">AIC211 · Chương 9 · Buổi 45</span>\n<h2>Buổi 45 — Basic Deep Learning and NLP for Cybersecurity</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14523 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO6, CLO7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO6, CLO7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Basic Deep Learning and NLP for Cybersecurity<br>- Fundamentals of Deep Learning and Neural Networks<br><br>+ Introduction to Neural Networks: Exploring the foundational concepts of Deep Learning.<br><br>+ Core Architectures and Mechanisms: Understanding the structure of Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLP), the role of activation functions, and the mechanics of the backpropagation algorithm.<br><br>+ Cybersecurity Applications: Reviewing basic theoretical frameworks and discussing practical directions for applying deep learning to security challenges.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>[Alpaydin2020] 12 Deep Learning<br>12.2 How to Train Multiple Hidden Layers (ReLU; Initialization; Backprop…)<br>12.4 Regularization (Weight Decay; Dropout)<br>12.5 Convolutional Layers (The Idea; Formalization)<br>12.7 Learning Sequences (Recurrent Networks; LSTM; GRU).<br><br>[Halder2018] Chapter 5<br>Featurization techniques… (TF-IDF; N-grams; Tokenization)<br>Using the Naive Bayes theorem to detect spam; Logistic regression spam filters.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Read the materials beforehand, attend classes, and fulfill the instructor's requirements.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
